      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5de9405aea7cc52772fcc359|full_name}: I'd prefer if it would do a periodic check regardless of what page the user is on. I expect most people (self included) will hang around the projects tab when managing multiple projects and neglect to switch to the home tab of the tool.\nThere currently isn't a compelling reason to regularly swap back to the home tab since it's just a \"welcome\"/version message. Most people will get busy and completely forget to check it if they leave VCC running all the time (again self included).\nSomething like a 30 minute interval (with once at tool startup) regardless of the active tab would be a better configuration. This would make it so it becomes one less thing that a developer has to keep in mind when making VRC stuff. Will also help prod people to staying on the latest version of the SDKs in general.\nAn analogy: It currently feels like we have to regularly click the webpage refresh button of a browser (switching to the home tab of the tool), even though things like polling and push notifications exist for SPAs (checking regardless of current tab).",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
